sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
A write route receives new data in the HTTP request body. Express must parse that JSON before a handler can use `req.body`.

```js
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

app.post("/api/events", (req, res) => {
  const incoming = req.body;
  return res.status(200).json({ received: incoming });
});
```

**Line by line:** `express.json()` is middleware, so it is registered before the POST route. When JSON arrives, Express stores the parsed JavaScript value on `req.body`. The route can then inspect that value.

Parsing and validation are separate responsibilities. Parsing turns the request body into JavaScript data. Validation decides whether that data is acceptable.

